After a weekend with hours of nh3.0.7, I have a couple of questions and
remarks.

First, I came across a dwarf. Ha, I thought, that might get me a
pick-axe. So I tried to attack it
	Do you really want to attack the dwarf [yn]?
Obviously, no. (Had not lost any luck yet, did not win any either). I
had noticed before that pets attack peaceful monsters, so I trapped the
dwarf between me and my kitten called Wiebertje..
	Wiebertje hits the dwarf --More--
	The dwarf hits Wiebertje! --More--
	Wiebertje is killed.
At that moment, I cried revenge:
	Do you really want to attack the dwarf [yn]?
I restrained myself. I still think that I had a very good reason to kill
it. Why doesn't nethack allow me to revenge my pets???

**** SPOILER ALERT (for those who haven't read this newsgroup lately) **
In a different game, toxic waste caused a polymorph into a blue dragon.
I had heard a rumour about baby dragons (and anyway, the command #sit
was suggested for laying eggs), so I #sat. I wasn't really ready to kill
my young, but ... I did my best to hatch them, but nothing happened.
I had dropped both eggs before I returned to human form. When I picked
them up again, they still were "two blue dragon eggs (laid by you)". I
thought: now I'm human again, I can #sit on the eggs without adding
another one. ("Having fun sitting on the ground?") When I picked the
eggs up again, they were just two eggs. I didn't quite believe it, but
when my kitten ate them later, I did.
So, how does one hatch an egg? Just by waiting?

Something else I noticed: when I throw darts in a shop, the shopkeeper
pays when I miss. In a supermarket, I threw large black knives, and the
shopkeeper did not pay. I had to pay, though, to get them back. Is this
a bug or a feature? Can anyone explain why?

